458 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Given these projections, the power usage of both Bitcoin mining and AI will continue to capture headlines. We believe, however, that policymakers and other stakeholders should pay more attention to how these new data centers are using power than to the absolute amounts of power they use. In the following section, we explain why, presenting our original research on the degree of actual flexibility of bitcoin miners and analyzing the impact of that flexibility on emissions.)
/E (Given these projections, the power usage of both Bitcoin mining and AI will continue to capture headlines. We believe, however, that policymakers and other stakeholders should pay more attention to how these new data centers are using power than to the absolute amounts of power they use. In the following section, we explain why, presenting our original research on the degree of actual flexibility of bitcoin miners and analyzing the impact of that flexibility on emissions.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
459 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Interconnection Queues Can Meet Increased Demand Data centers and Bitcoin are 6.3% of proposed new operational generation capacity.)
/E (Interconnection Queues Can Meet Increased Demand Data centers and Bitcoin are 6.3% of proposed new operational generation capacity.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
460 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The high-end estimate for data centers \(including AI\) is about 80 GW by 2027, while our estimate \(outlined above\) for Bitcoin mining suggests 18 GW by 2027. Combined, this represents 6.3 percent of the total generation capacity with a proposed operational date by the end of 2026. Indeed, the Berkeley Lab report shows growth in active generation projections have a remarkably similar exponential trend to data center demand.)
/E (The high-end estimate for data centers \(including AI\) is about 80 GW by 2027, while our estimate \(outlined above\) for Bitcoin mining suggests 18 GW by 2027. Combined, this represents 6.3 percent of the total generation capacity with a proposed operational date by the end of 2026. Indeed, the Berkeley Lab report shows growth in active generation projections have a remarkably similar exponential trend to data center demand.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [9]
>>
